\f0\b\fs36 \cf0 \strokec2 1. Self Join\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\fs24 \cf0 Definition
\f1\b0 \
A 
\f0\b Self Join
\f1\b0  joins a table with itself.\uc0\u8232 Used when rows in the same table are related.\
Example: customers from the same country.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f2\fs26 \cf0 \
SELECT \
c1.first_name AS customer1,\
c2.first_name AS customer2,\
c1.country\
FROM Customers c1\
JOIN Customers c2\
ON c1.country = c2.country\
AND c1.customer_id < c2.customer_id;\
\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f1\fs24 \cf3 \strokec3 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa298\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs36 \cf0 \strokec2 2. Aggregation Filtering\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\fs24 \cf0 Definition
\f1\b0 \
Filtering results 
\f0\b after aggregation
\f1\b0  using 
\f0\b HAVING
\f1\b0 .\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f2\fs26 \cf0 \
SELECT customer_id, SUM(amount) AS total_spent\
FROM Orders\
GROUP BY customer_id\
HAVING SUM(amount) > 500;\
\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f1\fs24 \cf3 \strokec3 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa298\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs36 \cf0 \strokec2 3. Duplicate Detection\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\fs24 \cf0 Definition
\f1\b0 \
Finding rows that appear more than once.\
Example: duplicate first names.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f2\fs26 \cf0 \
SELECT first_name, COUNT(*)\
FROM Customers\
GROUP BY first_name\
HAVING COUNT(*) > 1;\
\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f1\fs24 \cf3 \strokec3 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa298\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs36 \cf0 \strokec2 4. Top N Per Group\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\fs24 \cf0 Definition
\f1\b0 \
Finding the 
\f0\b top N rows within each group
\f1\b0 .\
Example: highest order per customer.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f2\fs26 \cf0 \
SELECT *\
FROM (\
SELECT \
customer_id,\
item,\
amount,\
ROW_NUMBER() OVER (PARTITION BY customer_id ORDER BY amount DESC) AS rnk\
FROM Orders\
) t\
WHERE rnk = 1;\
\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs24 \cf0 ROW_NUMBER
\f1\b0 \
Assigns a unique sequential number to rows in a partition.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf3 \strokec3 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa298\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs36 \cf0 \strokec2 5. Ranking\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\fs24 \cf0 Definition
\f1\b0 \
Assigning a rank based on order.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f2\fs26 \cf0 \
SELECT\
item,\
amount,\
RANK() OVER (ORDER BY amount DESC) AS rank\
FROM Orders;\
\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs24 \cf0 RANK
\f1\b0 \
Rows with equal values receive the same rank.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf3 \strokec3 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa298\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs36 \cf0 \strokec2 6. Window Functions\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\fs24 \cf0 Definition
\f1\b0 \
A 
\f0\b window function
\f1\b0  performs calculations across rows related to the current row without collapsing rows.\
Example: total orders per customer.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f2\fs26 \cf0 \
SELECT\
customer_id,\
amount,\
SUM(amount) OVER (PARTITION BY customer_id) AS total_customer_spend\
FROM Orders;\
\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f1\fs24 \cf3 \strokec3 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa298\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs36 \cf0 \strokec2 7. Running Totals\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\fs24 \cf0 Definition
\f1\b0 \
Cumulative sum over ordered rows.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f2\fs26 \cf0 \
SELECT\
order_id,\
amount,\
SUM(amount) OVER (ORDER BY order_id) AS running_total\
FROM Orders;\
\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f1\fs24 \cf3 \strokec3 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa298\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs36 \cf0 \strokec2 8. Gap and Island Problems\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\fs24 \cf0 Definition
\f1\b0 \
Finding 
\f0\b continuous sequences (islands)
\f1\b0  or 
\f0\b missing values (gaps)
\f1\b0 .\
Example: detect gaps in order IDs.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f2\fs26 \cf0 \
SELECT\
order_id,\
order_id - ROW_NUMBER() OVER (ORDER BY order_id) AS grp\
FROM Orders;\
\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f1\fs24 \cf0 Rows with same 
\f2\fs26 grp
\f1\fs24  belong to same island.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf3 \strokec3 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa298\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs36 \cf0 \strokec2 9. Hierarchical Queries\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\fs24 \cf0 Definition
\f1\b0 \
Queries that represent 
\f0\b parent-child relationships
\f1\b0  (tree structures).\
Example table structure:\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f2\fs26 \cf0 \
employee_id | manager_id\
\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f1\fs24 \cf0 Query pattern:\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f2\fs26 \cf0 \
SELECT *\
FROM employees\
START WITH manager_id IS NULL\
CONNECT BY PRIOR employee_id = manager_id;\
\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f1\fs24 \cf3 \strokec3 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa298\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs36 \cf0 \strokec2 10. Recursive CTE\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\fs24 \cf0 Definition
\f1\b0 \
A 
\f0\b Recursive CTE (Common Table Expression)
\f1\b0  repeatedly references itself to traverse hierarchies.\
CTE = temporary result set used inside a query.\
Example hierarchy:\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f2\fs26 \cf0 \
WITH RECURSIVE org AS (\
    SELECT employee_id, manager_id\
    FROM employees\
    WHERE manager_id IS NULL\
    \
    UNION ALL\
    \
    SELECT e.employee_id, e.manager_id\
    FROM employees e\
    JOIN org o\
    ON e.manager_id = o.employee_id\
)\
SELECT * FROM org;\
\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f1\fs24 \cf3 \strokec3 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa298\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs36 \cf0 \strokec2 11. Subquery Filtering\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\fs24 \cf0 Definition
\f1\b0 \
Using results of another query to filter rows.\
Example: customers who placed orders.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f2\fs26 \cf0 \
SELECT *\
FROM Customers\
WHERE customer_id IN (\
    SELECT customer_id\
    FROM Orders\
);\
\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f1\fs24 \cf3 \strokec3 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa298\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs36 \cf0 \strokec2 12. Conditional Aggregation\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\fs24 \cf0 Definition
\f1\b0 \
Aggregation based on conditions using 
\f0\b CASE
\f1\b0 .\
Example: count orders above 500.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f2\fs26 \cf0 \
SELECT\
SUM(CASE WHEN amount > 500 THEN 1 ELSE 0 END) AS large_orders,\
SUM(CASE WHEN amount <= 500 THEN 1 ELSE 0 END) AS small_orders\
FROM Orders;\
\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f1\fs24 \cf3 \strokec3 \
